  "status": "Original negative-index control reproduces invalid read/SIGSEGV. Guarded method passes warning-free Release/Debug and packaged-helper controls with actual RPM compiler flags; complete updated Node builds remain required.",
  "root_cause": "TimeZoneIdFromIndex handles UTC=0, then leaves id uninitialized if a negative internal index skips the enumeration loop. Its subsequent pointer check and string construction read the indeterminate value. GetTimeZoneIndex can represent not-found with -1; ordinary Temporal constructors validate names and DCHECK the result, so this is an internal boundary defect, not a demonstrated JavaScript-accessible failure.",
  "fix": "CHECK_GT(index, 0) after the UTC return enforces the one-based non-UTC enumeration contract before allocation/lookup. Existing end-of-enumeration checks remain unchanged. No warning suppression or arbitrary default value.",
  "proof": {
    "valid_checks": 20416,
    "zones": 637,
